<title>DENMARK: Danish Jan North Sea gas production rises 35 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish Jan North Sea gas production rises 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from its North Sea fields rose 35 percent in January 1997 to 748 million cubic metres from 554 million cubic metres in December 1996, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>    (Million cubic metres)   Jan 97    Dec 96   Jan 96</p>
<p>    Total production	     748	554	 538</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the third-biggest producer in western Europe after Norway and Britain.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom 45-33-969656</p>
